{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SimulationModule"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SimulationModule","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"SimulationModule"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Simulations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration"],"title":"Simulations"},{"anchor":"Time","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"],"title":"Time"},{"anchor":"States","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"],"title":"States"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" owns a world and a set of schedules, each named by a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". You add"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"systems to the schedules by label, then call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" once a frame with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time that passed. The simulation decides which schedules run:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" runs once, before the first frame."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs once for every fixed timestep of time that has passed, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics and other rate-sensitive rules advance by the same amount each run, however uneven the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frames are."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs once a frame.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and systems:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double }","struct FixedSteps: Resource { var count = 0 }","enum GameState: States { case menu, playing, paused }","","\/\/\/ Moves each entity by its velocity over one fixed timestep.","@System","struct Physics {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>, _ fixedTime: ResourceReader<FixedTime>) {","        let seconds = fixedTime.value.timestep \/ .seconds(1)","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx * seconds","        }","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Counts the runs of the schedule it is in.","@System","struct CountSteps {","    func run(_ steps: ResourceWriter<FixedSteps>) {","        steps.value.count += 1","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Spawns a ball at the origin.","@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(commands: inout Commands) {","        commands.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example runs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Physics"},{"type":"text","text":" on a fixed timestep of 1\/64 second, the default. A frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of 50 milliseconds covers three whole timesteps, so the ball moves three times:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","","var simulation = Simulation(world)","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics() }","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\""]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"States","anchor":"States"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A state type is a type, usually an enumeration, that conforms to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": the screens of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game, or the phases of a simulation. Add one to a simulation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". The simulation keeps the current state in the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource; to change it, a system sets "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and the change applies at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next frame. Entering, leaving and moving between states run schedules of their own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a run condition that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in one state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example spawns a ball on entering the ","type":"text"},{"code":"playing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state and moves it only while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"game is in that state:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var simulation = Simulation()","simulation.add(state: GameState.menu)","simulation.add(to: .onEnter(GameState.playing)) { SpawnBall() }","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics().runIf(inState(GameState.playing)) }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","simulation.world.resources[NextState<GameState>.self].set(.playing)","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.resources[CurrentState<GameState>.self].state)","\/\/ Prints \"playing\"","for (_, position) in simulation.world.query(Position.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\"","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/simulationmodule"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/startup":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once, before the first frame."}],"type":"topic","title":"startup","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/startup","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"startup"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","text":"ScheduleLabel"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/fixedUpdate":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once for each fixed timestep of elapsed time."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fixedUpdate"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV"}],"title":"fixedUpdate","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/fixedupdate","type":"topic"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/States":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/states","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"States","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"States","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"States","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type whose values are the states a simulation can be in.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/add(state:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds a state type to the simulation, starting in the given state."}],"type":"topic","title":"add(state:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/add(state:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"add"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"state"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onTransition(from:to:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation changes from one given state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to another.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"onTransition(from:to:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/ontransition(from:to:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"onTransition"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/update":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/update","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"update","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"update","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once a frame."}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"type":"topic","title":"SimulationModule","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","role":"collection"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onEnter(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation enters the given state."}],"type":"topic","title":"onEnter(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/onenter(_:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/Simulation